# What graphify leaves out of the knowledge graph (https://github.com/Graphify-Labs/graphify).
# Same syntax as .gitignore. graphify already skips everything in .gitignore (node_modules, dist,
# website/_site, video renders...); this file adds what's tracked in git but is data or pictures, not code.

# graphify's own output
graphify-out/

# pictures, video, fonts, documents: no code relationships, and reading them costs vision tokens
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.mp4
*.webm
*.wav
*.mp3
*.pdf
*.woff
*.woff2
*.ttf
*.otf
*.ico
*.icns
docs/loader.svg
docs/geekoc/*.svg

# generated data: big JSON the app reads, not code (the code that reads it stays in the graph)
src/mygeeky/data/*.json
mobile/src/data/*.json
tools/protocol_model/*.jsonl
tools/protocols/*.json

# lock files and build output
mobile/package-lock.json
package-lock.json
mobile/android/
mobile/ios/
mobile/.expo/

# the video's fonts and icon drawings (the scripts that make the poster, gallery and video stay)
launch/video/fonts/
launch/video/promise-icons/

# font licences
*-OFL.txt
OFL.txt

# private notes
ideas.md
future.md
